          "code": "END",
          "id": "end",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "END"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Flow Switch"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "ASSET_EXECUTION": "1772604626452",
            "STARTER_QUES": "1772029673604",
            "HELP": "1776949563732",
            "CLASSIFIED_MESSAGE": "1778736615109",
            "BOOK_LIST": "1780482207394"
          },
          "code": "FLOW_SWITCH",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1772447814530",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772447814532_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.USER_INPUT_ENTRY_POINT.$output.Intent}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "User Input Processor"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777359864407"
          },
          "code": "USER_INPUT_PROCESSOR",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1772447906621",
          "id": "1771235213181",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771235213182_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a structured data extraction agent.\n\nYour task is to determine the values for:\n- bookTypeCode\n- userQuestion\n- searchParameter\n- searchIdentifier\n\nFollow the instructions strictly and in the exact order given.\n\n---------------------------------------\nSTEP 1: Determine Source (Image vs Text)\n---------------------------------------\n\nIF {{Object.keys(context.$nodes.FILE_CONTENT_EXTRACTOR.$output).length != 0}} THEN\nUse values from:\nsearchIdentifier= {{$context.$nodes.FILE_PROCESSOR.$output.searchIdentifier}}\nbookTypeCode = {{$context.$variables.bookTypeCode}} \nElse:\nUse values from:\nsearchIdentifier= {{$context.$nodes.PROMPT_INPUT_PROCESSOR.$output.searchIdentifier}}\nbookTypeCode = {{$context.$variables.bookTypeCode}} \n\n---------------------------------------\nSTEP 2: Capture User Question\n---------------------------------------\n\nuserQuestion = {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n---------------------------------------\nSTEP 3: Resolve bookTypeCode\n---------------------------------------\n\nDetermine bookTypeCode using this priority order:\n\n1. If bookTypeCode is empty/null at this point, get it from chat-history: \n - bookTypeCode: {{$context.$nodes.GETALLVARIABLE.$input.bookTypeCode}}\n\n2. If still not found, extract bookTypeCode from the userQuestion/{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n- User can enter book type code in any case but always consider UPPER CASE, For example: (book OPS CORP , ops corp book , JPN RRF CORP book)\n- DO NOT populate book keyword, just  populate book name.\n\n---------------------------------------\nSTEP 5: Set Search Parameter\n---------------------------------------\n\nConvert {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} to lowercase before matching.\n\nSet searchParameter only when the input contains one of these exact terms as whole words:\n\n1) IF {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} contains - tag numbers, tags etc.\n   - Set searchParameter = TAG_NUMBER\n\n2) IF {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} contains - serial numbers, serials etc.\n   - Set searchParameter = SERIAL_NUMBER\n\n3) IF {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} contains - description, desc etc.\n   - Set searchParameter = DESCRIPTION\n\n4) IF {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} contains - assets, asset numbers, asset etc.\n   - Set searchParameter = ASSET_NUMBER\n\n5) for all other keywords based search\n    Set searchParameter = ALL\n\nImportant rules:\n- Match only the search keywords above.\n- Do not infer searchParameter from book names, corp names, country codes, or any other words.\n- If none of the exact keywords are present, keep searchParameter = \"ALL\".\n- Do not use \"book\" as a signal for searchParameter.\n\nMost importantly - If the input contains only book-related text such as \"ops corp book\", \"jpn rrf corp book\", or similar, do not change searchParameter.\n\nExamples:\n * show me the list with 01 in ops corp book. → ALL\n * show me the list with 01 in jpn rrf corp book. → ALL\n\n---------------------------------------\nOUTPUT FORMAT\n---------------------------------------\n\nReturn:\n\n{\n  \"bookTypeCode\": \"<value or null>\",\n  \"searchParameter\": \"<value>\",\n  \"userQuestion\": \"<value or null>\",\n  \"searchIdentifier\":\"<value>\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"searchIdentifier\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"searchParameter\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"userQuestion\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"bookTypeCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "switchBasedOnUserQues"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "Show asset details for a book": "1772450714891",
            "Show current period activity for a book": "1772533643441",
            "Show the list of books available for inquiry": "1778666806451"
          },
          "code": "SWITCHBASEDONUSERQUES",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1772029673604",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772029673605_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "User Input Entry Point"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776409555194"
          },
          "code": "USER_INPUT_ENTRY_POINT",
          "id": "1772449284758",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772449284759_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a Book Access inquiry classifier, intent router, and entity extractor for Oracle Fusion Fixed Assets.\n\nUser Input: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nStep 1 — Normalize\nCreate normalizedInput by:\n1. trimming leading and trailing spaces\n2. collapsing multiple spaces into one\n3. converting to lowercase\n\nKeep the original user input unchanged for final output.\n\nStep 2 — Intent detection\nSet Intent using this exact priority order.\n\nA. HELP\nIf the entire message is a help, greeting, assistance, capability, usage, supported-inquiry, example, starter-guidance, explanation, clarification, rephrasing, summarization, troubleshooting, error-help, next-step, contact-support, or simplification request\n\nThis includes but is not limited to:\n- help\n- hi\n- hello\n- how are you?\n- what can you do?\n- how can you help?\n- how do I use this?\n- show help\n- need help\n- give me examples\n- what questions can I ask?\n\nThen:\n- Intent = HELP\n\nB. STARTER_QUES\nIf normalizedInput exactly equals one of:\n- show asset details for a book\n- show current period activity for a book\n- show the list of books available for inquiry\n\nThen:\n- Intent = STARTER_QUES\n\nC. BOOK_LIST\nIf the entire message asks which books are available, accessible, allowed, or in scope for the user, then:\n- Intent = BOOK_LIST\n\nThis includes access-check questions for a book, such as whether the user can view, open, read, or access a book.\n\nD. ASSET_EXECUTION\nIf the entire message is a supported fixed asset inquiry for one book, one asset, one transaction, or one attached/current asset context, then:\n- Intent = ASSET_EXECUTION\n\nSupported inquiry families include:\n- Book period inquiries: current open period, current period activity, current period snapshot, or open period details for a book.\n- Asset list inquiries: list, search, find, or filter assets in a book by asset number, tag number, serial number, description, or text match.\n- Asset list operators: starts with, starting with, begins with, ends with, ending with, contains, containing, equals, equal, equal to.\n- Single asset inquiries: asset details, descriptive details, financial details, depreciation details, deprn details, distribution details, cost, original cost, date placed in service, prorate date, NBV, net book value, or supported single asset attributes.\n- Transaction list inquiries: recent transactions, recent additions, recent retirements, recent transfers, recent adjustments, or recent transaction details for a book.\n- Single transaction inquiries: details for a specific transaction number.\n- Book-level amount inquiries: total cost added, total cost retired, total reserve retired, total NBV retired, maximum transaction amount, or related transaction amount totals for current period, current fiscal year, this fiscal year, or a specific period.\n- Image or attachment inquiries: requests such as \"show me details for this asset\" when the message refers to the attached, uploaded, current, or visible asset.\n\nUse semantic meaning, not exact question wording. Do not require the user question to match a predefined sample.\n\nE. Otherwise\n- Intent = CLASSIFIED_MESSAGE\n\nImportant:\n- HELP and STARTER_QUES apply only when the entire message exactly matches one of the allowed phrases.\n- Do not assign HELP or STARTER_QUES when the message contains extra text, mixed intent, or unrelated content.\n- A standalone book name, book alias, or short book-like phrase is relevant and should not be classified as irrelevant.\n- If the input is short and appears to be a book name, book alias, or book candidate, treat it as a fixed-assets inquiry candidate unless the message clearly contains unrelated content.\n\nStep 3 — Classification\nUse exactly one final classification value.\n\nAllowed classification values:\n- HELP\n- STARTERQUEST\n- bookAccess\n- assetExecution\n- isRelevantbutnotinscope\n- isIrrelevantquestion\n\nRules:\n- If Intent = HELP, classification = HELP\n- If Intent = STARTER_QUES, classification = STARTERQUEST\n- If Intent = BOOK_LIST, classification = bookAccess\n- If Intent = ASSET_EXECUTION, classification = assetExecution\n\nIf Intent = CLASSIFIED_MESSAGE:\n- Use isRelevantbutnotinscope when the message is about Oracle Fusion Fixed Assets, book access, assets, asset transactions, asset books, or a likely fixed asset candidate, but asks for unsupported process, workflow, setup, maintenance, creation, update, delete, correction, transfer execution, retirement execution, posting, or action steps.\n- Use isIrrelevantquestion when the message is unrelated to books or fixed assets, casual conversation beyond HELP, general knowledge, content generation, or mixed intent that is not primarily a book or fixed asset inquiry.\n\nStep 4 — Operational constraints\nIf any of these are violated, set Intent = CLASSIFIED_MESSAGE and classification = isRelevantbutnotinscope:\n- Only one book may be queried per request.\n- Multiple books in a single request are not supported.\n- Maximum asset count returned is 10.\n- Asset update/create/delete actions are not supported.\n- Transaction execution actions are not supported.\n\nStep 5 — Entity extraction\nOnly extract entities when classification is not isIrrelevantquestion.\n\nbookTypeCode:\n- detect book / bookTypeCode / book type code / in book\n- detect forms such as \"book OPS CORP\", \"OPS CORP book\", \"in book OPS CORP\"\n- also detect a standalone book name, book alias, or likely book candidate when the entire input is just a book candidate\n- if the input is only a book candidate and no other entity is present, set bookTypeCode to the full input in uppercase\n- if missing, use {{$context.$variables.bookTypeCode}}\n- if still missing, return null\n- return the full book name in uppercase\n- do not include the word \"book\"\n\nsearchIdentifier:\n- for asset inquiries, extract the actual asset number, tag number, serial number, description value, or asset identifier\n- for asset list searches, extract only the pattern/search value after starts with, ends with, contains, equals, or similar operator\n- for single transaction inquiries, extract only the transaction number\n- do not include field names, operators, or book names\n- if missing, use {{$context.$variables.searchIdentifier}}\n- if still missing, return null\n\ntransactionTypeCode:\nAllowed values:\n- Addition\n- Adjustment\n- Transfer\n- Retirement\n\nExtraction rules:\n- If the input mentions addition, additions, added, or cost added, return Addition.\n- If the input mentions adjustment or adjustments, return Adjustment.\n- If the input mentions transfer or transfers, return Transfer.\n- If the input mentions retirement, retirements, retired, cost retired, reserve retired, NBV retired, or net book value retired, return Retirement.\n- If the input asks for generic recent transactions without a specific transaction type, return null.\n- Otherwise return null.\n\nStep 6 — Final output\nReturn only this JSON:\n\n{\n  \"userQuestionStarter\": \"<original input>\",\n  \"classification\": \"<HELP | STARTERQUEST | bookAccess | assetExecution | isRelevantbutnotinscope | isIrrelevantquestion>\",\n  \"Intent\": \"<HELP | STARTER_QUES | BOOK_LIST | ASSET_EXECUTION | CLASSIFIED_MESSAGE>\",\n  \"transactionTypeCode\": <value or null>,\n  \"searchIdentifier\": <value or null>,\n  \"bookTypeCode\": <value or null>\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"classification\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"bookTypeCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"searchIdentifier\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"transactionTypeCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Intent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"userQuestionStarter\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Starter Question2 Processor"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "STARTER_QUESTION2_PROCESSOR",
          "id": "1772450714891",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772450714892_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "The display output should be like this : \n\n<div style=\"background:#f9fafb; padding:12px 16px;\">\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;\">\n    I am happy to help. Just share the book name and your search details. I’ll remember the book name for the rest of our conversation. For example :\n</div>\n\n   \n<div style=\"margin-left: 22px; margin-bottom: 6px;\">\n</div>\n  <div\n    style=\"\n      font-weight: 500;\n      font-size: 12px;\n      padding: 1px 4px;\n      border-radius: 3px;\n      border: 1px solid #d1d5db;\n      background-color: #f9fafb;\n      display: inline-block;\n    \"\n  >\n    \"show me list of assets that ends with [search string] in [book name] book\"\n  </div>\n<div style=\"background:#f9fafb;\">\n\n- IF chatCounter <= 2 then render below HTML content: \n      <div style=\"font-family:'Oracle Sans'; font-size:12px; margin:12px 0; background:#f9fafb;\">\n            Type 'HELP' to know about my capabilities.\n      </div>\n </div>\nFollow this  rule strictly : \nDo not print any extra text or give results in the form of a code."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Starter Question3 Processor"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "STARTER_QUESTION3_PROCESSOR",
          "id": "1772533643441",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772533643442_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Output format should be like this :\n\n<div style=\"background:#f9fafb; padding:12px 16px;\">\n<div style=\"font-size:14px;\">\n    I am happy to help. Just share the book name. I’ll remember the book name for the rest of our conversation. For example :\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"margin-left: 22px; margin-bottom: 6px;\">\n</div>\n  <div\n    style=\"\n      font-weight: 500;\n      font-size: 12px;\n      padding: 1px 4px;\n      border-radius: 3px;\n      border: 1px solid #d1d5db;\n      background-color: #f9fafb;\n      display: inline-block;\n    \"\n  >\n    \"VISION CORP\"\n  </div>\n<div style=\"background:#f9fafb;\">\n\n- IF chatCounter <= 2 then render below HTML content: \n      <div style=\"font-family:'Oracle Sans'; font-size:12px; margin:12px 0; background:#f9fafb;\">\n            Type 'HELP' to know about my capabilities.\n      </div>\n</div>\nFollow this  rule strictly : \nDo not print any extra text or give results in the form of a code."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "File Content Extractor",
            "toolCode": "ORA_MULTI_FILE_PROCESSOR_TOOL"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772604713905"
          },
          "code": "FILE_CONTENT_EXTRACTOR",
          "id": "1772604626452",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772604638760",
              "name": "conversationId",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$workflow.$conversationId}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "TOOL"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "userAttachmentFound"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1772604924841",
            "false": "1772605056452"
          },
          "code": "USERATTACHMENTFOUND",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1771235213181",
          "id": "1772604713905",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772604713909_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{Object.keys($context.$nodes.FILE_CONTENT_EXTRACTOR.$output).length != 0}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "File Processor"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771235213181"
          },
          "code": "FILE_PROCESSOR",
          "id": "1772604924841",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772604924848_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role:\nYou are an asset number and book extraction agent.\n\nInput:\nOCR text extracted from an uploaded image:\n{{$context.$nodes.FILE_CONTENT_EXTRACTOR.$output}}\n\nGoal:\nExtract:\n1. searchIdentifier = asset number, tag number, serial number, or asset description\n2. bookTypeCode = OPS CORP\n\nRules for searchIdentifier:\n- Scan the OCR text only.\n- Extract the number (if there is no book, book type code etc before the number)\n- Keep the value exactly as found in the OCR text, including letters, numbers, hyphens, and slashes.\n- Do not invent or infer a value.\n\nOutput format:\n{\n  \"searchIdentifier\": \"<value>\",\n  \"bookTypeCode\": \"<value or null >\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"searchIdentifier\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"bookTypeCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Prompt Input Processor"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771235213181"
          },
          "code": "PROMPT_INPUT_PROCESSOR",
          "id": "1772605056452",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772605056458_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an value extractor Agent:\n\nExtract transactionTypeCode from {{$context.$nodes.USER_INPUT_ENTRY_POINT.$output.transactionTypeCode}}\nExtract bookTypeCode from  {{$context.$variables.bookTypeCode}}\nExtract searchIdentifier from {{$context.$variables.searchIdentifier}} \n \nLLM should return Book (bookTypeCode), Asset Number (assetNumber) and Transaction Type Code (transactionTypeCode) as output:\nOutput: \n{\n\t\"transactionTypeCode\": <value or null>,\n\t\"searchIdentifier\": <value or null>,\n\t\"bookTypeCode\": <value or null>\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"transactionTypeCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"searchIdentifier\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"bookTypeCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "setInitialVariables"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779429966017"
          },
          "code": "SETINITIALVARIABLES",
          "id": "1776409555194",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1782302496447",
              "name": "selectQueryDetails",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "SELECT\n      b.assetId,\n      b.bookName,\n      b.assetNumber,\n      b.description,\n      b.prorateDate,\n      b.datePlacedInService,\n      b.depreciateFlag,\n      b.originalCost,\n      b.cost,\n      b.recoverableCost,\n      b.creatingTransactionId,\n      b.salvageValueAmount,\n      b.salvageType,\n      b.salvageValuePercent,\n      b.methodName,\n      b.lifeInMonths,\n      b.periodFullyReserved,\n      b.periodFullyRetired,\n      a.assetId,\n      a.assetNumber,\n      a.currentUnits,\n      a.tagNumber,\n      a.manufacturerName,\n      a.serialNumber,\n      a.modelNumber,\n      a.assetType,\n      a.categoryConcatenatedSegment,\n      a.description,\n      b.ineffectiveDate\n    FROM assetFinancial b, assetDetails a"
            },
            {
              "id": "1782302485228",
              "name": "filterForAssetList",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "object",
              "value": "{\n  \"filter_entity\": [\n    \"bookName\",\n    \"assetNumber\",\n    \"description\",\n    \"prorateDate\",\n    \"datePlacedInService\",\n    \"depreciateFlag\",\n    \"cost\",\n    \"recoverableCost\",\n    \"periodFullyReserved\",\n    \"periodFullyRetired\",\n    \"tagNumber\",\n    \"manufacturerName\",\n    \"serialNumber\",\n    \"modelNumber\",\n    \"assetType\",\n    \"categoryConcatenatedSegment\"\n  ]\n}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1777274360054",
              "name": "bookTypeCode",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{[$context.$nodes.USER_INPUT_ENTRY_POINT.$output.bookTypeCode, $context.$nodes.SETINITIALVARIABLES.$input.bookTypeCode, $context.$variables.bookTypeCode].find(v => v && v !== \"null\" && v !== \"<null>\" && v !== \"\")}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1777274318365",
              "name": "searchIdentifier",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{[$context.$nodes.USER_INPUT_ENTRY_POINT.$output.searchIdentifier, $context.$nodes.SETINITIALVARIABLES.$input.searchIdentifier, $context.$variables.searchIdentifier].find(v => v && v !== \"null\" && v !== \"<null>\" && v !== \"\")}}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1776409582461",
              "name": "FaInqChatCounter",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "integer",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.FaInqChatCounter + 1}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "help_html",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "let assetHtml = `<div style=\"background:#f9fafb; padding-left:12px;\">\n\n&nbsp\n<div style=\"font-size:14px; line-height:1.5; color:#111827;\">\n\n  <div style=\"font-size:16px; font-weight:600; margin-bottom:6px;\">\n    Fixed Asset Inquiry Assistant\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom:12px; color:#4b5563;\">\n    This assistant helps you quickly understand and resolve questions about fixed assets. You can inquire about asset details, cost, depreciation balances including YTD depreciation, period depreciation, accumulated depreciation, reserve, and net book value, along with key attributes such as units, employee, location, and assignment.\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"font-weight:600; margin-bottom:4px;\">Before you start</div>\n\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom:12px; color:#374151;\">\n    For the best user experience, manually resize the assistant window to full screen.\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"font-weight:600; margin-bottom:4px;\">How to use this agent</div>\n\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom:12px; color:#374151;\">\n    1. Submit a question requesting a specific type of information such as asset details, depreciation details, retirement details, transactions, or net book value and the assistant will respond with the corresponding data.<br>\n    2. You can search by asset number, book name, asset description, or other supported asset attributes depending on the question.<br>\n    3. In addition to text prompts, this assistant can also process attachments and images to help produce results.\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"font-weight:600; margin-bottom:6px;\">\n    Find books you can access\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom:6px; color:#374151;\">\n    To see which asset books you have access to in this assistant, use this command:\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px; border:1px solid #d1d5db; background:#f9fafb; padding:4px 6px; border-radius:4px; display:inline-block; margin-bottom:12px;\">\n    \"show me the books I have access to\"\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"font-weight:600; margin-bottom:6px;\">\n    How to phrase a question to get the right asset information\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">\n    You can specify a search-parameter operator using one of the supported operators listed below:\n  </div>\n\n  <ul style=\"margin-top:4px; margin-bottom:10px; padding-left:20px; color:#374151;\">\n    <li>starts with</li>\n    <li>ends with</li>\n    <li>contains</li>\n    <li>equal</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">Examples</div>\n\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px; border:1px solid #d1d5db; background:#f9fafb; padding:4px 6px; border-radius:4px; display:inline-block; margin-bottom:6px;\">\n    \"show me list of assets that starts with [search string] in [book name] book\"\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px; border:1px solid #d1d5db; background:#f9fafb; padding:4px 6px; border-radius:4px; display:inline-block; margin-bottom:6px;\">\n    \"show me list of assets that contains [search string] in [book name] book\"\n  </div>\n\n  <br>\n\n  <div style=\"font-size:12px; border:1px solid #d1d5db; background:#f9fafb; padding:4px 6px; border-radius:4px; display:inline-block; margin-bottom:6px;\">\n    \"show me list of assets that ends with [search string] in [book name] book\"\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"color:#4b5563; margin-bottom:12px;\">\n    These commands return a list of assets in a specific book based on the search condition.\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"font-weight:600; margin-bottom:6px;\">\n    Supported questions\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom:6px; color:#374151;\">\n    You can ask questions such as:\n  </div>\n\n  <ul style=\"margin-top:4px; margin-bottom:10px; padding-left:20px; color:#374151;\">\n    <li>\"show me details for asset [asset number]\"</li>\n    <li>\"show me depreciation details for asset [asset number] in [book name] book\"</li>\n    <li>\"show me net book value for asset [asset number] in [book name] book\"</li>\n    <li>\"show me cost details for asset [asset number] in [book name] book\"</li>\n    <li>\"show me recent retirement details of book [book name]\"</li>\n    <li>\"show me transactions for asset [asset number] in [book name] book\"</li>\n    <li>\"show me assets assigned to employee [employee name]\"</li>\n    <li>\"show me assets for location [location name]\"</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <div style=\"font-weight:600; margin-bottom:6px;\">\n    Functionality not currently supported\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom:6px; color:#374151;\">\n    This assistant does not currently support:\n  </div>\n\n  <ul style=\"margin-top:4px; margin-bottom:10px; padding-left:20px; color:#374151;\">\n    <li>Creating, updating, transferring, retiring, or deleting assets</li>\n    <li>Posting accounting entries or depreciation</li>\n    <li>Changing asset assignments, locations, employees, or units</li>\n    <li>Approving transactions or workflow actions</li>\n    <li>Providing access to books or assets that you are not authorized to view</li>\n    <li>Answering questions outside fixed asset inquiry and related asset information</li>\n  </ul>\n\n  <br>&nbsp;\n</div>\n</div>`;\n\nreturn assetHtml;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776949589395"
          },
          "code": "HELPHTML",
          "id": "1776949563732",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
