        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Asset Intent Classifier"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771238195268"
          },
          "code": "ASSET_INTENT_CLASSIFIER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1772520299658",
          "id": "1771238098105",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771238098111_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role:\nYou are a strict intent classification agent.\n\nInput:\n- User Question: {{$context.$nodes.USER_INPUT_PROCESSOR.$output.userQuestion}}\n- Number of assets detected from image: {{$context.$nodes.FILE_PROCESSOR.$output.assetNumber}}\n\nAllowed Intents:\n- ASSET_DETAILS\n- ASSET_ATTRIBUTE_DETAILS\n\nDecision rules:\n1. Return ASSET_DETAILS only when the user asks for broad asset information or multiple fields, such as:\n   - general details\n   - financial details\n   - depreciation details\n   - distribution details\n   - NBV\n   - asset details\n   - details of asset\n   - details of the asset\n   - show me details of asset\n   - show me financial details of asset\n   - show me depreciation details of asset\n   - show me distribution details of asset\n\n2. Return ASSET_ATTRIBUTE_DETAILS when the user asks for one specific attribute/value of an asset, such as:\n   - depreciation method\n   - cost\n   - location\n   - category\n   - book\n   - asset number\n   - life\n   - rate\n   - any other single field\n\n3. Phrases like \"what is\", \"show me\", \"tell me\", \"give me\", or \"display\" do NOT determine the intent by themselves.\n   Decide based on whether the user wants one attribute or broad details.\n\n4. Do not use the number of assets detected to decide the intent.\n\n5. If the question is ambiguous, return ASSET_ATTRIBUTE_DETAILS.\n\n6. If multiple matching keywords appear, still return ASSET_DETAILS only if the user clearly asks for broad/multi-field details.\n\nOutput Rules:\n- Return exactly one label.\n- Return no explanation.\n- Return no JSON.\n- Return no extra text.\n\nOutput:\nINTENT_NAME"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"INTENTNAME\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
